WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.525
An offspring is a young living thing produced by a parent.

00:00:04.525 --> 00:00:08.500
In these activities, we are mainly talking about baby animals.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.212
A parent is an adult that has offspring.

00:00:11.212 --> 00:00:16.725
The words describe a relationship: this young animal is the offspring of that adult.

00:00:16.725 --> 00:00:19.388
As a baby grows, it becomes an adult.

00:00:19.388 --> 00:00:23.650
It does not remain a baby forever or become a different kind of animal.

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:27.433
Some baby animals have special names.

00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:29.333
A baby horse is a foal.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:31.283
A baby sheep is a lamb.

00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:33.108
A baby duck is a duckling.

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:38.683
Notice that a duckling and an adult duck are the same kind of animal, even though one is smaller.

00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:40.283
A duck hatches from an egg.

00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:44.383
A horse is born from its mother rather than hatching from an egg.

00:00:45.542 --> 00:00:49.167
A baby tiger is called a cub, not a chick or a tadpole.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:54.554
A chick is a young bird, while a tadpole belongs to the frog life cycle in your worksheet.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.592
A caterpillar belongs to the butterfly life cycle.

00:00:57.592 --> 00:01:01.142
In a matching activity, read both columns carefully.

00:01:01.142 --> 00:01:06.542
A familiar baby name is only correct when it is paired with the right adult animal.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.112
A baby monkey often looks similar to its parent but is smaller.

00:01:12.112 --> 00:01:17.575
Similar means that some features are alike; it does not mean every feature is identical.

00:01:17.575 --> 00:01:23.888
For a short written answer, name a feature: a baby horse and its parent both have four legs.

00:01:23.888 --> 00:01:27.562
For a difference, you could say the baby horse is smaller.

00:01:27.562 --> 00:01:30.962
Use an example that matches the animals you are comparing.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:36.954
You now have two tools: special baby names and careful comparisons.

00:01:36.954 --> 00:01:39.792
Most baby animals are smaller than their parents.

00:01:39.792 --> 00:01:45.504
Some look similar, while others, like a tadpole and an adult frog, look very different.

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:51.804
In the activity, match each adult to its young, then write one similarity and one difference.

00:01:51.804 --> 00:01:56.329
There can be more than one good written answer if you support it with evidence.
